</header>

<main>
<!-- ================= HERO ================= -->
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="t">
  <div class="wrap hero-grid">
    <div class="rv">
      <span class="eyebrow">Case Study · E-commerce · WordPress</span>
      <h1 id="t">Madina <em>Clothing</em></h1>
      <p class="lead">An Islamic lifestyle store — modest wear, Arabian fragrances and spiritual essentials — turned into a mobile-first WooCommerce shop with a <strong>custom-built Shoppable Reel plugin</strong> that sells straight from video.</p>
      <dl class="meta">
        <div><dt>Client</dt><dd>Madina Clothing</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Market</dt><dd>United Kingdom · £</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Platform</dt><dd>WordPress + Woo</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Design · Dev · Plugin</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://madinaclothing.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit live store
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M7 17 17 7M9 7h8v8"/></svg></a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#solution">See the solution</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="stage rv" id="stage" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="stage-inner" id="stageInner">
        <span class="orb gold" style="width:54px;height:54px;right:22%;top:-6px;animation-delay:-3s"></span>
        <span class="ring" style="width:110px;height:110px;left:-30px;bottom:-20px"></span>
        <span class="arch" style="right:-6px;bottom:-30px;transform:rotate(8deg) scale(.8)"></span>
        <div class="laptop">
          <div class="laptop-screen"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Madina Clothing desktop homepage"></div>
          <div class="laptop-base"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="phone"><div class="phone-screen" role="img" aria-label="Madina Clothing mobile homepage scrolling"></div></div>
        <div class="chip chip-1"><i>◆</i><span><b>158</b> products live</span></div>
        <div class="chip chip-2"><i>▶</i>Custom reel plugin</div>
        <div class="chip chip-3"><i>❖</i><span><b>16</b> categories</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= SECTION 01 — WHY / PROBLEM ================= -->
<section class="block challenge" aria-labelledby="s1">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <span class="sec-num">01</span>
      <span class="eyebrow">Why this site</span>
      <h2 id="s1">A real shop with a mixed catalogue — and customers living on their phones.</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="rv" style="color:var(--ink-2);max-width:760px;margin:-8px 0 26px">Madina Clothing runs a physical store in the UK and sells across Facebook, Instagram, TikTok and WhatsApp. They needed one place where a shopper could find a product, check the size, ask a question and pay — on mobile, without sending a single DM.</p>

    <div class="problems">
      <article class="problem tilt rv">
        <span class="tag">Problem 01</span>
        <h3>Selling through DMs</h3>
        <p>Prices, stock and sizes were answered one chat at a time. That doesn't scale, and orders were lost at night and weekends.</p>
        <div class="fix">A self-serve shop with PayPal checkout, open 24/7</div>
      </article>
      <article class="problem tilt rv">
        <span class="tag">Problem 02</span>
        <h3>A very mixed catalogue</h3>
        <p>Abayas in S-52 / M-54 / L-56, thobes, kufis, perfumes in ml, bakhoor burners, Qurans, prayer mats — each type needs different data.</p>
        <div class="fix">16 nested categories plus variable products</div>
      </article>
      <article class="problem tilt rv">
        <span class="tag">Problem 03</span>
        <h3>Size doubt = returns</h3>
        <p>Modest-wear buyers worry about length and fit. Without a size guide and a quick way to ask, they leave or return.</p>
        <div class="fix">Size chart popup + WhatsApp &amp; phone, one tap away</div>
      </article>
      <article class="problem tilt rv">
        <span class="tag">Problem 04</span>
        <h3>Shoppers start on video</h3>
        <p>Customers discover products on reels, but a normal product page doesn't feel like the video they just watched.</p>
        <div class="fix">A custom Shoppable Reel plugin, built from scratch</div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="reqs rv">
      <span class="orb"></span>
      <h3>Client requirements</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>150+ SKU WooCommerce catalogue</li><li>Size variations &amp; size guide</li><li>Mobile app-like navigation</li>
        <li>WhatsApp + phone chat</li><li>Secure PayPal checkout</li><li>Wishlist &amp; compare</li>
        <li>AJAX filters &amp; quick view</li><li>Video reels linked to products</li><li>Owner edits pages himself (Elementor)</li><li>Premium, calm Islamic look</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= SECTION 02 — SOLUTION & IMPACT ================= -->
<section class="block solution" id="solution" aria-labelledby="s2">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <span class="sec-num">02</span>
      <span class="eyebrow">Solution &amp; impact</span>
      <h2 id="s2">A customised Woodmart build, plus a plugin made only for this shop.</h2>
    </div>

    <!-- Signature feature -->
    <div class="hero-feature rv">
      <div style="position:relative;z-index:1">
        <span class="badge-custom">★ Custom plugin · v1.5.0</span>
        <h3>Shoppable Reel by DevSazzad</h3>
        <p>I wrote this WordPress plugin from scratch (PHP + vanilla JS) so the store can sell directly from vertical video, the way its customers already shop.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li><span><strong>Reels carousel</strong>, each reel linked to a WooCommerce product with its thumbnail, live price, discount badge and a "Go to product" button.</span></li>
          <li><span><strong>Fullscreen modal player</strong> with prev/next, keyboard controls, a sound toggle, share and a side playlist.</span></li>
          <li><span><strong>Floating mini-reel</strong> pinned to the product gallery. You can drag it with touch or mouse, expand it or minimise it.</span></li>
          <li><span><strong>Built to be reliable</strong>: it uses the YouTube IFrame API so mute and autoplay behave consistently, and a MutationObserver so it also works inside the Elementor editor.</span></li>
        </ul>
<div class="code"><span class="c">// sr-frontend.js — dependable playback</span>
<span class="k">loadYouTubeAPI</span>().then(YT =&gt; new YT.Player(id, {
  playerVars:{ autoplay, mute: muted ? 1 : 0 },
  events:{ onReady: e =&gt; e.target.playVideo() }
}));</div>
      </div>
      <div class="reel-stage" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="reel r2"><div class="play"></div></div>
        <div class="reel r3"><div class="play"></div></div>
        <div class="reel r1">
          <span class="snd">🔊</span><div class="play"></div>
          <div class="reel-ui"><div class="t">Royal Elegance Abaya<small>£110.00</small></div><span class="go">SHOP</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Feature grid -->
    <div class="features">
      <article class="feat tilt rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="14" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="3" y="14" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="14" y="14" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Category architecture</h3>
        <p>16 categories in a nested mega-menu: Men's › Thobe · Kufi · Moroccan Thobes, and Lifestyle › Quran · Bakhoor Burners · Frames · Books.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feat tilt rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 7h18M3 12h18M3 17h10"/><path d="M17 15l2 2 3-4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Size guide &amp; variations</h3>
        <p>Variable products with S-52 / M-54 / L-56 lengths and a size-chart popup on every garment, so buyers ask fewer questions and return less.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feat tilt rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="6" y="2" width="12" height="20" rx="3"/><path d="M10 18h4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>App-like mobile UX</h3>
        <p>A sticky bottom toolbar (Home · Shop · Cart · Account · Menu), off-canvas filters and a two-column product grid that's easy to use with your thumb.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feat tilt rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 12a8 8 0 0 1-11.6 7.1L4 20l1-5A8 8 0 1 1 21 12z"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Trust &amp; contact</h3>
        <p>A floating WhatsApp + phone widget, a trust block (UK store, premium quality, UK support, secure delivery) and social links in the header.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feat tilt rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m20 20-3.5-3.5"/></svg></div>
        <h3>AJAX shop experience</h3>
        <p>Price filter, show 9/12/18/24 products, grid switcher, sorting, quick view, wishlist and compare. None of it reloads the page.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feat tilt rv">
        <div class="ico"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="6" width="18" height="13" rx="3"/><path d="M3 10h18M7 15h3"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Checkout &amp; ownership</h3>
        <p>WooCommerce PayPal Payments for secure checkout. A Woodmart child theme and Elementor let the owner update banners and pages himself.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- Gallery -->
    <div class="gallery">
      <figure class="shot rv"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Product page with size guide, wishlist and compare"><figcaption>Product page <span>Size guide · variations</span></figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="shot rv"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="AJAX shop archive with price filter"><figcaption>Shop archive <span>AJAX filters</span></figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="shot rv"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Moroccan Thobes category page"><figcaption>Category <span>Moroccan Thobes</span></figcaption></figure>
